          "id": "overview",
          "title": "Overview",
          "descriptions": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "On January 29, 2019, Michael Anthony Roy was arrested for shoplifting at a Home Depot in American Fork. According to his "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "federal complaint",
                  "url": "/records/pacer/michael-anthony-roy-lawsuit-complaint.pdf#page=5"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "Detective Shawn Lott",
                  "url": {
                    "$ref": "entity-officer-page-shawn-e-lott",
                    "$path": [
                      "url"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": " offered him a deal to work off the charges by becoming a confidential informant for the Utah County Major Crimes Unit. Roy accepted and was released that day."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "The next day, officers mistook Roy for another person during an operation at an Orem gas station. A subsequent "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "investigative report",
                  "url": "/records/pacer/michael-anthony-roy-lawsuit-exhibit-1-internal-affairs-investigative-report.pdf#page=3"
                },
                {
                  "text": " found that Lott recognized Roy from their encounter the day before but failed to tell the other officers they had the wrong person."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "Officers tried to pull Roy from his vehicle while his seat belt remained fastened. After Lott released the belt, officers pulled him out, and Sergeant Doug Howell struck him with a rifle, causing a head injury requiring four staples. The "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "report’s findings",
                  "url": "/records/pacer/michael-anthony-roy-lawsuit-exhibit-1-internal-affairs-investigative-report.pdf#page=27"
                },
                {
                  "text": " documented policy violations, including a unanimous use-of-force board finding that Howell’s use of the firearm as a compliance tool was outside policy."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "The "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "investigative report",
                  "url": "/records/pacer/michael-anthony-roy-lawsuit-exhibit-1-internal-affairs-investigative-report.pdf#page=5"
                },
                {
                  "text": " states that investigators could not find "
                },
                {
                  "format": "bold",
                  "text": "usable body-camera footage from any officer at the scene"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", including Lott."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "formatted-text",
              "segments": [
                {
                  "text": "Roy later sued, and the defendants agreed to a combined "
                },
                {
                  "format": "link",
                  "text": "$93,000 settlement",
                  "url": "/records/spanish-fork-city/michael-anthony-roy-settlement-agreement-utah-county-american-fork-and-spanish-fork.pdf"
                },
                {
                  "text": " without admitting liability."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
